    "result_text": "There's only one test class in the suite (`AcceptanceTest`), and it passes. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `timezone` field derived from the owner's region via the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\n**Changes (3 files):**\n\n1. **`RegionTimezone.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, cohesive class following the existing per-derived-field pattern (`MembershipLevel`, `CheckDigit`, `AgeBand`, \u2026). Its single `of(owner)` method reuses `CustomerCodes.region(owner)` and maps the region to the IANA name: `NSW->Australia/Sydney`, `VIC->Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD->Australia/Brisbane` (null otherwise).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line wiring `timezone` to `RegionTimezone.of(owner)`, exactly mirroring the adjacent `locality` mapping.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `timezone` schema property so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field.\n\n**Why this keeps structural impact low:** the derivation lives in a brand-new class with zero surrounding methods (WMC_other \u2248 0), so it pays nothing for context. I avoided adding a method to `CustomerCodes` (which carries `build`/`deduplicate`/`region`/`hash8` complexity) or growing any existing function \u2014 the only touched method is the mapper interface stub (CC 1), extended by a single annotation. Region logic is reused rather than duplicated.",
